From: RK3128 reference <reference@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] lima: return after the unreachable varying formats

The varying format of MR !37449 ends in assert(0) with no return: a build with
-Db_ndebug=true (the board's) has no assert, and Mesa's own -Werror=return-type
stops it ("control reaches end of non-void function"). Return 0 after the assert.
---
diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/lima/lima_draw.c b/src/gallium/drivers/lima/lima_draw.c
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/lima/lima_draw.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/lima/lima_draw.c
@@ -970,6 +970,7 @@
    case LIMA_VARYING_TYPE_VEC4_UNORM8:
    default:
       assert(0);
+      return 0;
    }
 }
 
